# Cursor Guides (Budgeter 2026 Frontend)

This file is a quick, project-specific reference for working in Cursor on `b-frontend`.

## Workflow constraints (project preference)

- Keep changes **minimal and localized** (avoid broad refactors unless explicitly requested).
- Prefer editing **one file at a time** (finish/verify, then move on).

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Vite runs on `http://localhost:5173/`.

## API base URL (dev vs production)

- **Dev (localhost)**: the frontend uses **same-origin** requests (no absolute base URL) and relies on the Vite dev proxy.
- **Production (Netlify)**: the frontend uses `VITE_API_BASE_URL`.

### Netlify env var

Set this in Netlify **before build** (Vite reads env vars at build time):

- `VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://dgloriaapi.co.uk`

## Dev proxy (avoid CORS on localhost)

In `vite.config.js`, we proxy API calls so the browser talks to `localhost:5173` and Vite forwards `/api/*` to your backend:

- Frontend calls: `fetch('/api/...')`
- Vite proxies to: `http://localhost:8081/api/...`

If you change `vite.config.js`, **restart** `npm run dev`.

## Auth model (Bearer token)

Backend endpoints are token-based:

- `POST /api/register` → returns `{ user, token }`
- `POST /api/login` → returns `{ user, token }`
- `GET /api/user` → requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- `POST /api/logout` → revokes the current token

Frontend behavior:

- Token is stored in `localStorage` under: `budgeter2026_auth_token`
- All API requests automatically include:
  - `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (when present)
  - `Accept: application/json`

Implementation:

- `src/api/api.js`: token storage + automatic `Authorization` header
- `src/view/LoginView.vue`: login + redirect
- `src/view/RegisterView.vue`: register + redirect
- `src/view/DashboardView.vue`: loads current user + logout

## CORS (Netlify → API)

If you see CORS errors on Netlify, it must be fixed on the **Laravel API** side:

- Allow the Netlify site origin(s) in `config/cors.php`
- Ensure `Authorization` header is allowed

Example symptom:

- API responds with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:3000` but the request is coming from `https://<your-site>.netlify.app`.

## Pages (routes)

Defined in `src/router/index.js`:

- `/` and `/login` → `LoginView`
- `/register` → `RegisterView`
- `/dashboard` → `DashboardView` (requires token)

## Mock-budget dashboard (Phase 1 starter)

The dashboard currently runs on locally persisted mock data (stored in `localStorage`) to support Phase 1 development before backend endpoints exist.

Dashboard UI is in `src/view/DashboardView.vue`.

